# The agent runs with a LOCAL model by default (apfel, Apple Intelligence on macOS 26+): no key, free, offline.
# Everything below is optional and only needed for the hosted Gemini model.
#
# Copy to .env (git-ignored). Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Optional: pin the Gemini model (default gemini-3.5-flash). The evaluation of 2026-11-12 used
# gemini-3.1-flash-lite, whose free tier has a larger daily quota (15 requests per minute).
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-lite
# Optional: space requests to stay under the free tier's per-minute limit (make eval-gemini sets 4.2s)
# GEMINI_MIN_INTERVAL=4.2s
# Optional: choose the provider: auto (default: apfel if installed, else Gemini) | apfel | gemini
# LLM_PROVIDER=auto
# Optional: use an apfel server that is already running (default: the agent starts its own on a free port)
# APFEL_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434

# Any other OpenAI-compatible server (Ollama, llama.cpp server, vLLM; works on Linux/Windows):
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434
# OPENAI_MODEL=llama3.1:8b
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# LLM_CONTEXT_TOKENS=0        # >0 trims tool results to fit a small window

# Chat webhook for the report (Slack-style incoming webhook, {"text": ...}); empty = report.md only.
# NOTIFY_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.slack.com/services/...
